# ===========================================================================
# 换行符策略 / Line-ending policy
# ===========================================================================
#
# 统一换行符：无论谁、在哪个系统克隆，工作区文件都是 LF。
# Normalize line endings: the working tree stays LF no matter who clones the
# repository or which system they are on.
#
# 为什么需要 / Why this matters:
#   git 的 core.autocrlf 是每台机器的本地设置，默认值因平台而异。
#   git's core.autocrlf is a per-machine local setting whose default varies by
#   platform.
#
#   没有这一行时，Windows 用户（autocrlf=true）克隆得到的会是 CRLF 文件，
#   与仓库中存储的 LF 不一致，会导致：
#     - diff 出现整文件变更 / whole-file diffs that hide the real change
#     - 测试快照失配 / mismatched test snapshots
#     - 换行符保真相关的断言基线不可靠
#       unreliable baselines for the line-ending fidelity assertions
#
#   Without this line, Windows users (autocrlf=true) get CRLF files while the
#   repository stores LF, which causes all of the above.
#
# 本项目所有源文件均为 LF，且插件本身会读写这些文件，因此显式锁定。
# Every source file here is LF, and the plugin itself reads and writes these
# files, so the policy is pinned explicitly.
#
# 本文件优先级高于 core.autocrlf，因此无需依赖任何人的本地设置。
# This file takes precedence over core.autocrlf, so nobody's local setting can
# change the outcome.

* text=auto eol=lf

# ===========================================================================
# 二进制文件 / Binary files
# ===========================================================================
#
# 不做任何换行符转换，避免损坏内容。
# No line-ending conversion at all, so the bytes are never corrupted.

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.pdf binary

# ===========================================================================
# Windows 脚本 / Windows scripts
# ===========================================================================
#
# 这些脚本必须使用 CRLF 才能被 cmd.exe / PowerShell 正确执行。
# These scripts require CRLF to run correctly under cmd.exe / PowerShell.

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
